course: dictionary
lesson: 7885
title: The rand: money in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they often give you clues to its meaning. Here the sentence says «one cost R20 (twenty rand, South African money)». The words in the brackets tell you that rand is money, and that it belongs to South Africa.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word. Does «one cost R20 (twenty South African money)» still make sense? It does, so rand must mean money.
explain: A capital letter can change the meaning. The rand with a small r is money. The Rand with a capital R, short for the Witwatersrand, is a place with gold mines near Johannesburg. The sentence and the topic tell you which one is meant.
fact: Rand means the money of South Africa.
fact: One rand is made of 100 cents.
fact: The symbol for the rand is R, as in «R50», and its currency code is ZAR.
fact: The Rand, with a capital R, is an area of ridges around Johannesburg, famous for its gold mines.
fact: (Rare) A rand is also a strip of leather in a shoe.
exercise: In «one cost R20 (twenty rand, South African money)», what is the rand? | A mountain in Cape Town | A family pet | *South African money | A type of shoe
exercise: How many cents make one rand? | 10 | *100 | 50 | 1000
exercise: The Rand, with a capital R, is an area famous for what? | Sandy beaches | *Gold mines | Sheep farms | Football stadiums
test: What is the symbol for the rand, as in «R50»? | Z | Ra | Rd | *R
test: In «three now cost R60», what does R60 mean? | *Sixty rand | Sixty cents | Six hundred rand | Six rand
exam: Which is the currency code for the South African rand? | RAND | SAR | *ZAR | R
